`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
Spring Boot 4's module split means many new "library" issues here are really thin facade modules (an annotation + a `ContextCustomizerFactory`) rather than new functionality — their SPI registration happens via `META-INF/spring/org.springframework.test.context.ContextCustomizerFactory.imports`, picked up automatically by `SpringFactoriesLoader`, so no native-image reflection config is typically needed for this *kind* of class.
A forge worktree directory often has a `forge/logs/<coordinate>/` trail and preserved `human-intervention` branches from earlier attempts at the *same* coordinate (even under a different issue number) — checking those first can save a full re-investigation, since Gradle test logs and `execution-metrics.json` are hard evidence, not guesses.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

